## Executive Summary
This project engineered an end-to-end security information and event management (SIEM) implementation for a healthcare practice migrating its on-premises Electronic Health Record (EHR) system (eClinicalWorks) and directory infrastructure (Azure Active Directory) into a hybrid cloud model. 

The primary business and regulatory objective was resolving critical HIPAA compliance gaps in centralized audit logging, real-time threat visibility, and ePHI data protection across hybrid endpoints and cloud services.

---

## Problem Statement & Regulatory Drivers
* **Lack of Centralized Audit Logging:** Prior on-premises infrastructure lacked consolidated security monitoring, failing to satisfy the mandatory audit controls required under the HIPAA Security Rule.
* **HIPAA Technical Safeguard Mandates (45 CFR § 164.312):** Requires covered entities to implement hardware, software, and procedural mechanisms that record and examine activity in information systems containing or using Electronic Protected Health Information (ePHI).
* **NIST SP 800-66r2 Alignment:** Used federal guidelines to map HIPAA administrative, physical, and technical safeguards directly to SIEM logging architectures.

