## Technical Solution & Implementation Architecture

[ On-Premises Servers & Endpoints ] ──( Azure Monitor Agents )──┐
│
[ Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) ] ──( Native Cloud Connectors )──► [ Azure Log Analytics Workspace ]
│                   │
[ eClinicalWorks Cloud EHR ] ──────────( Secure API / Log Ingestion )─┘                   ▼
[ Microsoft Sentinel SIEM ]
│
┌───────────────────────┴───────────────────────┐
▼                                               ▼
[ KQL Detection & Alert Logic ]                [ RBAC & Defensible Audit Trails ]


### 1. Centralized Log Ingestion & Cloud Workspace
* Provisioned an **Azure Log Analytics Workspace** configured for encrypted ingestion and long-term retention of audit trails.
* Deployed **Azure Monitor Agents** across local clinical endpoints and servers to forward system, access, and security event logs to Sentinel.
* Configured native **Azure Active Directory (Azure AD)** connectors to stream authentication, privileged role escalations, and directory changes in real time.

### 2. Detection Rules, Threat Analytics & RBAC
* Developed custom KQL (Kusto Query Language) correlation queries to detect account anomalies, brute-force patterns, and suspicious access to ePHI.
* Implemented strict **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)** within Microsoft Sentinel to ensure only authorized security personnel have visibility into system audit logs.

### 3. Procedural Framework & Operational Handover
* Structured rollout using the **EDO4SIEM** (Evaluation, Deployment, Operation for SIEM) waterfall methodology.
* Authored standard operating procedures (SOPs), incident escalation runbooks, and staff training guides to enable independent operational maintenance and audit readiness.

